    "body": "\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nFix MXFP4 model startup with --moe-backend flashinfer_moe_ep_cutedsl. During post-load setup, the CuTeDSL path can leave the source scale attributes as None; megakernel setup then tries to assign .data on None.\r\n\r\nOn main, the startup failed at the old .data assignment with `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'data'.`\r\n\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Register missing megakernel weight parameters with the existing replace_parameter helper.\r\n- Preserve direct .data rebinding for parameters that already exist, keeping all four model parameters aliased to the megakernel buffers without copying.\r\n- Add a regression test for MXFP4 CuTeDSL routed-expert startup.\r\n- The regression came from #62326. PR changed the rebinding code to assign through .data, assuming the scale parameters already existed. MXFP4 preparation can set those parameters to None, which caused the startup error.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- `pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_fi_moe_ep.py -q` — 22 passed.\r\n\r\ngsm8k validation:\r\n\r\n```\r\nvllm serve RedHatAI/GLM-5.3-MXFP4 \\\r\n  --host 0.0.0.0 \\\r\n  --port 18000 \\\r\n  --trust-remote-code \\\r\n  --max-model-len 8192 \\\r\n  --reasoning-parser glm45 \\\r\n  --data-parallel-size 4 \\\r\n  --enable-expert-parallel \\\r\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.95 \\\r\n  --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3 \\\r\n  --moe-backend flashinfer_moe_ep_cutedsl\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\npython tests/evals/gsm8k/gsm8k_eval.py \\\r\n  --num-questions 1319 \\\r\n  --num-shots 5 \\\r\n  --max-tokens 1024 \\\r\n  --host http://127.0.0.1 \\\r\n  --port 18000 \\\r\n  --use-chat-completions \\\r\n  --reasoning-effort low \\\r\n  --max-concurrency 32 \\\r\n  --seed 42\r\n```\r\n\r\nAccuracy 0.9477\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n\r\n`process_weights_after_loading` binds the adapter’s kernel weights back to the model layer. For MXFP4 CuTeDSL, the scale attributes can be None at this point, so assigning through .data raises an exception. The change registers only missing parameters with replace_parameter; existing parameters retain the current direct rebinding behavior.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
